Qwen3.5 MTP: the untied draft embedding and lm_head go on the meta device.

Qwen3_5MTP builds its own embed_tokens (VocabParallelEmbedding) and lm_head
(ParallelLMHead), each vocab_size x hidden_size: 248,320 x 5,120 on
Qwen3.8-27B, 2.37 GiB each in bf16. Both proposer paths replace them with the
target's after loading. load_eagle_model (v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/eagle/
utils.py) shares when the draft has no has_own_embed_tokens / has_own_lm_head
set; _maybe_share_embeddings / _maybe_share_lm_head (v1/spec_decode/
llm_base_proposer.py) share for a draft without those attributes. The
embedding is shared only without pipeline parallelism. Qwen3_5MTP.load_weights
never calls process_eagle_weight, so the flags stay unset. Until the
replacement the two copies hold device memory. On a GGUF target the plugin's
MTP adapter maps only the nextn block, so they are never filled; on a
safetensors target load_weights copies the target's embed_tokens and lm_head
tensors into them.

When the copy is replaced anyway (embedding: pipeline-parallel world size 1;
lm_head: last rank) and the head is neither tied to the embedding nor untied
by the checkpoint (word_embeddings_untied_by_checkpoint), the module is built
on the meta device without the quant_config, so it takes the unquantized
embedding method. While those modules are in place, load_weights skips the
checkpoint tensors under model.embed_tokens. and lm_head.; on a safetensors
target the weight iterator still reads them (into host memory with the default
iterators, into device memory with fastsafetensors and instanttensor). Once the
target's modules have replaced them, load_weights passes those tensors on as
before. Every other case keeps the previous construction. The truncated draft
head of qwen3_5-mtp-draft-vocab (model.draft_lm_head) is built and loaded as
before.

Tested on a mixed checkpoint built for its smaller MTP head:
Qwen3.8-27B-GSQ-RCO-IQ3_S-mtp.gguf with its nextn block (blk.64) taken from
Qwen3.8-27B-IQ4_XS-3.84bpw.gguf, 177.5 MB (IQ3_XXS, IQ4_XS, Q5_K) instead of
348.5 MB (Q6_K). With the patch it boots and serves under SPEC=mtp with the
torch allocator capped at 15.99 GiB (per_process_memory_fraction). Draft
acceptance, bench/labd_accept.py --chunk 32 at DRAFT_TOKENS=3: 3.630 tokens
per step against 3.656 for the unmodified file.

Cut against the tree the whole series leaves: qwen3_5_mtp.py is last touched
by qwen3_5-mtp-draft-vocab.

